# One configuration file for the whole book. Copy to `.env` at the repository
# root; every chapter's compose stack reads it and will not start without it.
#
# Pick ONE of the four model blocks below — uncomment it and comment out the
# default. This sets the model most agents use. (Some chapters also run
# specific components on local models by design; those chapters start Ollama
# themselves, and this choice does not affect them.)

# --- Choice 1 (default): Gemini — free tier at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.7-flash

# --- Choice 2: OpenAI
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini

# --- Choice 3: Claude
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5

# --- Choice 4: Ollama — free local models, no key. The first start downloads
#     the model (about 2 GB), then it is cached. Note: in Docker, Ollama runs
#     on the CPU on macOS — containers cannot reach Apple GPUs. Setup for all
#     three Ollama variants: "Local models with Ollama" in README.md.
# LLM_MODEL=ollama_chat/llama3.2
# OLLAMA_ENABLED=1
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://ollama:11434

# --- Choice 4 on an NVIDIA GPU (Linux / Windows WSL2 with the NVIDIA
#     container toolkit): use OLLAMA_GPU=1 in place of OLLAMA_ENABLED=1;
#     everything else stays the same.
# LLM_MODEL=ollama_chat/llama3.2
# OLLAMA_GPU=1
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://ollama:11434

# --- Choice 4 on a Mac with an Apple GPU (or any machine with Ollama
#     installed natively): install from https://ollama.com, run
#     `ollama pull llama3.2`, then use these two lines — the stack calls the
#     host's Ollama, which uses the GPU on its own.
# LLM_MODEL=ollama_chat/llama3.2
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# The four blocks above are examples of the most common providers. Any provider that LiteLLM
# supports (https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers) works the same way — its
# key variable plus the model string, e.g. DEEPSEEK_API_KEY= and
# LLM_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-chat. Providers with OpenAI-compatible APIs also
# work via LLM_MODEL=openai/<model> with OPENAI_API_BASE=<their endpoint>.
